para(d,"Untestable from the package: tariff or change-in-law pass-through on the Nomad price (Exhibit C terms not provided); the AFUDC rate (assumed about 7% on CWIP); Station 496 outage-window premium (no outage plan; Haugland item 24 puts affected hours at a 1.70 factor instead of 1.35); FEOC and ITC eligibility effect on net cost.",size=9.5,color=GRAY)
d.add_heading("Risk-register audit",1)
para(d,"Curation tells present: all twelve values are round numbers; no basis column populated; no item exceeds contingency; no probability or correlation; every item is a cost overrun, none is a scope or decision risk. Exposure arithmetic: register $5.3M plus contingency $2.28M equals $7.58M on Station 360, 17.9% of approval level less reserves. The element-level Monte Carlo needs $3.4M (base) to $6.2M (wide) to reach P80; the reference-class uplift median is +31%. The register is adequate against its own element ranges and thin against outside history. Double-count: the $1.0M material and tariff risk overlaps both the fixed battery price and the 3% per year escalation already in the lines. Missing families: siting denial as a decision risk, commissioning-window ownership, counterparty, concurrent-project resource competition, FEOC.")
d.add_heading("Pre-mortem",1)
para(d,"It is June 2031. Hyde Park BESS went into service in March 2030, fifteen months late, at $74M. The ZBA hearing in late 2027 drew the abutters who had raised open-land and traffic concerns since 2024; the Board conditioned approval on a redesigned screening plan and a smaller footprint, which sent the civil package back through Haugland in the winter of 2028. The borings, finally drilled in the spring of 2027, found debris deeper than the 2014 closure set showed, and the platform went from 2.5 ft of fill to a piled solution; the Haugland reconciliation that had never been done was done in a change order. Nomad's twelve containers arrived on schedule in January 2028 and sat in a rented yard for nine months, with the remote-support clock and the warranty extension running from Final Acceptance dates that kept moving. Station 496's relay cutovers needed night outage windows the estimate had priced at straight time. AFUDC alone added $4M. The full-funding PAF had said Conceptual, -25/+50%, but everyone remembered $57M.",italic=True)
table(d,["Early-warning indicator","Would current controls catch it?"],[["Geotech report not issued by IFC-civil design freeze (mid-2027)","No: no P6 gate ties IFC to the report"],["ZBA hearing date not set within 90 days of Article 80 filing","No: siting carries hours, not milestones"],["HEG reconciliation not closed before the PAF is drafted (Nov 2026)","Only if the CoE makes it a PAF precondition"],["Nomad final-drawings milestone (13 Jul 2026 in C-2) slipped","Partly: payments tracked, not the downstream effect on GSU spec and civil"],["Station 496 outage plan not issued before construction pricing","No"]],widths=[3.6,3.1],font=9)
d.add_heading("What would change our mind",1)
table(d,["Challenge","Retiring evidence"],[["KS1 / #1","Signed HEG-to-Rev 3 scope map showing the gap is 24211 and platform scope already in E, with the residual under $2M"],["KS2 / #2, #9","Article 80 filed, ZBA calendar in hand, P6 showing at least 3 months of float on the siting chain, System Planning memo on spot generation ownership"],["KS3 / #3, #4, #5","Geotech report, crew build-up for battery install, HMA fixing the footprint; then Class 3 with -15/+25%"],["#6","Two EMA relay-replacement actuals within 30% of $362K per relay"],["#7","Exhibit C clause showing tariff or change-in-law pass-through; otherwise remove or re-label"],["#8","Range-estimating session output with P50/P80 per item and stated correlation"],["#13","The ten primary sources verified; reference class re-run"]],widths=[1.4,5.3],font=9)
d.add_heading("Certification",1)
para(d,"Tested: the layer extraction arithmetic (reconciles), the benchmark placement, the risk and contingency sizing against both an element Monte Carlo and outside base rates, seven stress scenarios, and the schedule logic as stated in the PAF. Not tested: Haugland's estimate itself, the Nomad commercial terms beyond pricing, the P6 logic, the geotechnical basis, and the internal indirect rates.")
para(d,"Bottom line: the $57.2M is defensible as a station cost and sits where a project of this size, duration and site should sit relative to public comparables; it is not yet defensible as a full-funding number, because the two items most likely to move it (the Haugland reconciliation and the siting path) are both open and both point up. Take the three defensible reductions (about $3M) only after the HEG map closes, present the November number as Class 4 with an honest dollar range, and put the geotech and HMA on the critical path now. Ready with repairs.",bold=True)
